  "seoTitle": "President Prabowo to Submit VP Nominees",
  "metaDescription": "President Prabowo Subianto must submit two vice presidential candidates to the MPR by November 25 following the resignation of Gibran Rakabuming Raka.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "President Prabowo Subianto is required to submit two candidates for vice president to the MPR by November 25, 2026.",
    "The official inauguration of the new vice president is scheduled to take place on December 9, 2026.",
    "Regional representative bodies have stated they will leave the final selection of the vice presidential candidate to the President."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Following the resignation of Gibran Rakabuming Raka from his position as Vice President of Indonesia, the political process to appoint a successor is underway. According to current regulations, President Prabowo Subianto must present two potential candidates to the People's Consultative Assembly (MPR) no later than November 25, 2026. While political parties such as PKS and Nasdem have indicated support for a candidate originating from the Gerindra Party, the Regional Representative Council (DPD RI) has stated it will defer entirely to the President's discretion in making the selection. The MPR is expected to announce the final two names prior to the upcoming plenary session, with the formal inauguration of the chosen official set for December 9, 2026. Discussions surrounding potential candidates remain ongoing as the legislative timeline progresses.",
